WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.133
[opening theme music playing]

01:48.024 --> 01:49.025
[music fades]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.116
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

02:00.328 --> 02:02.747
[intriguing instrumental music playing]

02:10.004 --> 02:11.756
[Chae-ok] My mother once showed me…

02:13.967 --> 02:16.094
the many different shapes you could make

02:17.303 --> 02:19.222
with just one single string.

02:21.099 --> 02:23.768
She told me to imagine
the many possibilities

02:24.894 --> 02:28.231
between two people
if their paths were to ever intertwine.

02:28.815 --> 02:31.025
The unpredictable moments of fate

02:32.068 --> 02:34.112
shaping a new path and direction

02:35.113 --> 02:36.656
that you would never expect.

02:38.825 --> 02:41.703
And for that one
seemingly coincidental encounter,

02:43.121 --> 02:44.914
our paths forever change,

02:45.498 --> 02:48.251
as the days, time, and space

02:49.669 --> 02:52.547
all conspire to move together
in the same direction.

02:54.674 --> 02:56.926
["Time" by Baek A playing]

02:57.010 --> 03:03.933
♪ Will it come when winter's gone… ♪

03:05.143 --> 03:07.729
It was an attraction
that seemed vague at first,

03:07.812 --> 03:09.731
but became crystal clear.

03:09.814 --> 03:12.984
♪ …when spring comes? ♪

03:13.067 --> 03:16.905
- ♪ Before the cherry blossoms fall… ♪
- [distant explosion]

03:16.988 --> 03:18.198
Though it defied logic,

03:19.282 --> 03:21.367
it became an immeasurable force.

03:21.451 --> 03:23.411
One that sweeps you off your feet.

03:24.120 --> 03:25.413
[distant explosion]

03:26.247 --> 03:27.457
[blows landing]

03:30.752 --> 03:31.753
[soldier 1 groans]

03:40.887 --> 03:43.431
[Chae-ok] A force
that pulls you closer and closer,

03:43.514 --> 03:45.350
until finally, you are together.

03:49.312 --> 03:50.897
That immeasurable force

03:51.856 --> 03:52.982
is the power of fate.

03:53.066 --> 03:54.275
[gunshot echoing]

04:02.325 --> 04:03.743
[suspenseful music playing]

04:07.121 --> 04:09.290
- [distant explosions echoing]
- [panting]

04:20.385 --> 04:21.427
I'm really sorry.

04:23.638 --> 04:25.348
Can you forgive me for being late?

04:26.266 --> 04:27.809
[breathing deeply]

04:33.147 --> 04:36.401
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN CAUSALITY AND FATE

04:36.484 --> 04:39.153
EPISODE 4
IMPRINTING

04:39.737 --> 04:41.781
- [phones ringing]
- [man 1] Do it now.

04:42.824 --> 04:43.658
Yes, sir.

04:43.741 --> 04:45.827
Did you find out
where the fireworks were set off?

04:45.910 --> 04:48.955
We think it was east of Namsan, sir.
It was near Ongseong Hospital.

04:49.038 --> 04:51.666
- [man 2] Look into it immediately.
- [man 3] Yes, sir.

04:52.792 --> 04:54.460
- Ongseong Hospital?
- Yes, sir.

04:55.670 --> 04:56.921
[ominous music playing]

05:00.216 --> 05:02.051
[man 1] They have to be
around here somewhere.

05:02.135 --> 05:04.387
Find the bastards
who set off the fireworks!

05:04.470 --> 05:05.471
[man 2] Yes, sir!

05:11.227 --> 05:12.186
[sniffs]

05:12.979 --> 05:14.355
[man 3] Over here, sir!

05:14.939 --> 05:16.149
[man 1] Ah, over there!

05:16.649 --> 05:17.608
[man 4] That way.

05:32.165 --> 05:34.709
- Tell me where he went. Where is he?
- I apologize, sir.

05:34.792 --> 05:37.670
I was following Master Jang,
then I lost him somehow and…

05:38.588 --> 05:40.256
Where did you lose Master Jang?

05:40.340 --> 05:43.009
Towards Bonjeong, Commissioner Ishikawa.
The third district, sir.

05:47.472 --> 05:50.683
- [man 1] No, no, it's on me.
- [man 2] Don't be crazy. I'm paying.

05:50.767 --> 05:52.435
- Hey, where are we?
- [yelps]

05:53.353 --> 05:54.979
- Excuse me.
- Hey. Watch it, huh?!

05:55.063 --> 05:56.689
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Don't touch me!

05:56.773 --> 05:58.483
- Let's go. Let's go.
- What the hell?

05:58.566 --> 06:00.943
Shouldn't you say sorry
if you bump into someone?

06:01.027 --> 06:03.488
[man 2] Forget about it.
Let's just go to another bar.

06:03.571 --> 06:05.448
[panicked breathing]

06:17.251 --> 06:19.670
- [Tae-sang sighs]
- How does it fit, sir?

06:19.754 --> 06:22.256
Everything is measured
exactly the way you wanted.

06:23.341 --> 06:24.717
It fits just right.

06:24.801 --> 06:27.678
I like the style.
Plus the fit looks quite good on me.

06:28.429 --> 06:29.430
Ah!

06:30.473 --> 06:31.808
Did you hurt yourself, sir?

06:31.891 --> 06:32.892
[pained grunt]

06:34.769 --> 06:35.728
[chuckles softly]

06:37.105 --> 06:37.939
Where's the rickshaw?

06:38.523 --> 06:40.400
It's out back. I'll show you now.

06:41.901 --> 06:43.569
[whimsical music playing]

06:46.155 --> 06:46.989
[sniffs]

06:47.490 --> 06:50.576
It should be big enough
to fit a person inside. Is that possible?

06:50.660 --> 06:52.286
Yes. When should I bring it?

06:52.370 --> 06:55.706
Come meet me behind the tailor shop
at 9:00 p.m. sharp. Is that clear?

06:58.084 --> 06:59.961
[driver] Will this be enough space?

07:03.756 --> 07:07.260
I'll return the rickshaw just as soon
as I'm done with it, all right?

07:09.929 --> 07:10.930
One more thing, sir.

07:18.271 --> 07:20.523
You be safe out there, Master Jang, okay?

07:24.318 --> 07:25.820
Commissioner Ishikawa,

07:26.529 --> 07:29.157
do you think that Master Jang
went inside of the hospital

07:29.240 --> 07:31.033
and got past all of the guards?

07:36.164 --> 07:37.165
That's right.

07:37.248 --> 07:40.960
I, Jang Tae-sang…
decided to break into Ongseong Hospital

07:41.043 --> 07:44.422
to protect the House of Golden Treasure
and the people I love,

07:44.505 --> 07:45.798
despite being injured.

07:45.882 --> 07:47.633
[intriguing music playing]

07:56.559 --> 07:59.312
[soft, pained grunting]

08:08.946 --> 08:10.114
[music fades]

08:13.659 --> 08:17.497
I heard that you are planning
to get someone out of Ongseong Hospital.

08:19.790 --> 08:21.626
And I want to help you out.

08:22.585 --> 08:26.130
- You could end up dead if you do this.
- I know. I want to help.

08:26.881 --> 08:27.882
I'm going with you.

08:27.965 --> 08:31.177
[scoffs] It's not
some fun adventure, you know.

08:31.260 --> 08:33.554
I was told
one of my comrades was arrested.

08:33.638 --> 08:34.972
He was taken there last night.

08:36.557 --> 08:39.936
Please, Tae-Sang, I won't get in your way.
Just get me inside.

08:40.770 --> 08:42.355
[sighs]

08:44.690 --> 08:47.568
The rickshaw can only hide one person,
and that's Myeong-ja.

08:48.069 --> 08:51.447
I can't promise to get you out.
You'll have to find a way out on your own.

08:52.198 --> 08:53.074
I understand.

08:53.157 --> 08:55.284
If you do happen to run into any trouble,

08:55.868 --> 08:58.913
I might not…
be able to help you, Jun-taek.

08:58.996 --> 09:00.540
It's every man for himself.

09:00.623 --> 09:03.751
Can you please just
think this over some more?

09:03.834 --> 09:06.796
This operation is dangerous, Master Jang.

09:07.713 --> 09:08.714
Listen here.

09:11.300 --> 09:12.385
My name is Jang Tae-sang.

09:12.468 --> 09:13.636
Enough of that already.

09:13.719 --> 09:16.055
Your name won't protect you
from bullets or sword attacks.

09:16.138 --> 09:19.475
Yeah? Well, I'm pretty nimble,
so don't be too worried, all right?

09:20.476 --> 09:22.395
- [Mrs. Nawol sighs]
- [chuckles softly]

09:27.233 --> 09:28.985
Just come back alive, Master Jang.

09:29.735 --> 09:31.779
When you do,
I'll have your favorite cognac ready.

09:35.116 --> 09:38.077
[clearing throat pointedly]

09:45.710 --> 09:46.627
We better get going.

09:50.965 --> 09:52.633
I risked my life to get here.

09:54.385 --> 09:55.428
[sighs]

09:56.971 --> 09:57.888
[Tae-sang sighs]

10:03.728 --> 10:05.396
This wasn't the plan, okay?

10:05.479 --> 10:07.356
You said that you found Myeong-ja.

10:07.440 --> 10:09.692
It was in the message you sent.
Why did you even say that?

10:09.775 --> 10:12.903
I meant I'd bring her to you
after you found a way out.

10:13.404 --> 10:15.364
You were supposed to send me
a signal from outside.

10:15.948 --> 10:16.824
[Tae-sang scoffs]

10:19.493 --> 10:20.703
Whatever. That's fine.

10:21.245 --> 10:24.248
Okay, let's say we both
miscommunicated about what the plan was.

10:24.332 --> 10:26.834
The kids though?
I'm sorry, that's something else.

10:26.917 --> 10:28.544
Who are these kids? Do you know?

10:28.628 --> 10:30.546
- I don't know.
- So what are you doing?

10:30.630 --> 10:33.591
You have no obligation to these kids.
Why did you bring them into this?

10:33.674 --> 10:36.177
What do you intend to even do?
Why did you do it?

10:37.219 --> 10:38.220
They needed saving.

10:41.098 --> 10:43.184
Otherwise they would've died in there.

10:46.729 --> 10:48.898
How about we discuss this downstairs, huh?

10:50.941 --> 10:53.235
It appears two of these guys
are dead already,

10:53.736 --> 10:56.489
and the rest won't be saying much
for a while, I think.

10:58.199 --> 11:00.951
All right, kids. Follow me.

11:01.577 --> 11:03.287
Here. [grunts]

11:03.788 --> 11:05.414
Come on. Let's go.

11:10.711 --> 11:11.629
[Tae-sang sighs]

11:25.184 --> 11:26.852
[breathing heavily]

11:30.690 --> 11:32.024
What is it? What's going on here?

11:32.858 --> 11:35.820
There's no evidence to suggest
anyone broke in from outside.

11:35.903 --> 11:38.948
We think
the kids probably did this by themselves.

11:39.782 --> 11:40.741
[inhales sharply]

11:43.953 --> 11:45.371
You better find them!

11:45.454 --> 11:49.041
I want everybody looking for the kids.
Everybody on it! You got that?

11:49.125 --> 11:49.959
Yes, sir!

11:50.710 --> 11:52.128
[ominous music playing]

11:52.211 --> 11:53.421
[breathing heavily]

11:54.380 --> 11:55.297
[music fades]

12:01.887 --> 12:03.973
What the hell is this? Where's Myeong-ja?

12:07.393 --> 12:08.561
I have no idea.

12:09.812 --> 12:11.731
And who the heck are these kids?

12:11.814 --> 12:13.149
I don't know that either.

12:13.816 --> 12:15.484
They were found in the laboratory.

12:16.861 --> 12:19.613
Laboratory?
They have one in this hospital?

12:20.614 --> 12:21.532
And who are you?

12:21.615 --> 12:22.992
Oh. [clears throat]

12:23.659 --> 12:25.536
Kwon Jun-taek.
Nice to meet you, whoever you are.

12:26.370 --> 12:28.831
Tae-Sang only told me a little
about why you guys are in here.

12:31.041 --> 12:32.793
And who is this Japanese guy?

12:37.089 --> 12:38.507
He works here at Ongseong Hospital.

12:38.591 --> 12:41.093
He doesn't look like he works here at all.

12:42.636 --> 12:43.846
How do I know he's trustworthy?

12:43.929 --> 12:45.973
The priority right now is Myeong-ja.

12:46.474 --> 12:48.851
Let's just focus
on the original plan for now.

12:48.934 --> 12:52.855
But first, we should probably discuss
what to do with these kids you have.

12:52.938 --> 12:56.776
What's this laboratory you mentioned?
Where is it, and what's it for?

13:03.157 --> 13:04.325
[dragging feet]

13:13.417 --> 13:14.835
[solemn music playing]

13:17.505 --> 13:19.840
I used to work at a gun factory.

13:20.466 --> 13:22.510
After that, the soldiers took me here.

13:23.385 --> 13:25.888
I've had injections every day since then.

13:26.430 --> 13:29.016
What were the injections for?
Do you know what they do?

13:29.099 --> 13:30.643
[girl] I don't know, sir.

13:31.435 --> 13:34.980
I saw that the other kids were all dying
from whatever they put in us.

13:36.273 --> 13:39.610
Some died after suffering
for a little while, or from a high fever.

13:40.486 --> 13:42.321
Some died in their sleep.

13:42.404 --> 13:45.324
Every day, I could hear
people screaming and crying.

13:45.407 --> 13:46.534
[breathes shakily]

13:47.910 --> 13:49.703
They didn't want to die like this.

13:51.539 --> 13:52.623
They were all just…

13:53.290 --> 13:55.417
just screaming and screaming.

13:58.838 --> 14:00.673
In Manchuria,
I witnessed something similar.

14:02.591 --> 14:04.009
What they did was pure evil.

14:04.093 --> 14:07.596
The experiments conducted
on those prisoners were absolutely insane.

14:10.266 --> 14:12.476
It looks like the same thing
is happening here.

14:17.648 --> 14:18.732
[sighs]

14:21.318 --> 14:22.528
[ominous music playing]

14:24.989 --> 14:28.075
Okay, so, um…
what are you trying to say, hmm?

14:28.158 --> 14:31.537
That, um… you think Myeong-ja could be
going through something similar?

14:32.246 --> 14:33.080
She could be.

14:33.163 --> 14:35.583
We should find her
as quickly as possible, then.

14:37.126 --> 14:39.795
If we delay this any longer,
something bad could happen to her.

14:39.879 --> 14:42.631
- We gotta get these kids out before--
- That's not my concern.

14:42.715 --> 14:45.634
You created this situation here,
so fix it yourself, huh?

14:46.635 --> 14:49.388
Are you really
about to abandon these kids right now?

14:58.772 --> 15:02.067
I don't expect you to understand,
but I have my own problems to deal with.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.570
If I don't get Myeong-ja
back to Ishikawa soon,

15:04.653 --> 15:07.448
I will lose everyone I love
and everything I've built here.

15:07.531 --> 15:10.534
I won't be guilt-tripped into helping you
get all these kids out of here.

15:10.618 --> 15:11.952
It's not why I came here.

15:12.036 --> 15:14.413
It's not okay that you're trying
to put me in this situation.

15:14.496 --> 15:17.166
It's too big of a risk for me.
I'm better off looking for Myeong-ja.

15:17.249 --> 15:18.083
[gasps]

15:19.543 --> 15:21.170
[Tae-sang breathing shakily]

15:27.134 --> 15:28.636
[mischievous music playing]

15:40.022 --> 15:41.440
[ominous music playing]

15:50.866 --> 15:52.242
We can't find them anywhere.

15:52.326 --> 15:55.412
I think it's possible
they might've found a way out of the ward.

15:55.496 --> 15:59.124
No, this hospital, it has too many guards.
They're still inside.

16:00.167 --> 16:01.710
Search every level again.

16:02.294 --> 16:04.171
They must be hiding in here somewhere.

16:04.755 --> 16:07.591
You know kids love
to play hide-and-seek, right?

16:07.675 --> 16:08.759
Yes, sir.

16:09.718 --> 16:10.844
[sighs]

16:10.928 --> 16:12.221
[tense music playing]

16:46.964 --> 16:48.215
[tense music building]

17:04.440 --> 17:06.316
I think we can fit two kids in this one.

17:06.400 --> 17:09.820
There's no time for that. Let's go
with the smallest first. You and you.

17:09.903 --> 17:10.821
And, uh…

17:12.281 --> 17:13.115
[screams]

17:14.533 --> 17:15.451
[shushing]

17:16.827 --> 17:18.287
[tense music building]

17:40.726 --> 17:41.602
[knocks on door]

17:44.938 --> 17:46.023
[knocking on door]

17:48.150 --> 17:49.193
[knocking on door]

17:54.782 --> 17:56.325
[suspenseful music playing]

18:07.086 --> 18:07.920
[music fades]

18:15.219 --> 18:16.386
[sighs]

18:19.932 --> 18:22.976
What's the matter, huh?
Did something scare you just now?

18:23.060 --> 18:24.269
[ominous music playing]

18:29.525 --> 18:30.359
It's okay.

18:59.304 --> 19:00.764
[ethereal music playing]

19:08.105 --> 19:09.273
[Chae-ok] What is this?

19:10.315 --> 19:11.525
What is his job here?

19:13.861 --> 19:16.572
Why would he draw
something like this in a hospital?

19:22.119 --> 19:23.287
Who is that man out there?

19:29.376 --> 19:30.294
He's Sachimoto.

19:33.005 --> 19:35.174
The guy you asked me to find for you.

19:36.508 --> 19:37.759
The painter Sachimoto.

19:44.266 --> 19:45.559
[dramatic music playing]

19:54.067 --> 19:55.652
[Jun-taek] What's that around your neck?

19:59.239 --> 20:00.908
An old present from my daughter.

20:02.367 --> 20:03.785
She was 12 when she made it.

20:03.869 --> 20:06.205
She was learning to carve wood
at the time.

20:07.414 --> 20:09.416
She gave me one necklace
and the other to her mom.

20:12.544 --> 20:16.048
If you don't mind me asking,
how'd you both end up becoming sleuths?

20:18.717 --> 20:22.721
We've been searching for my wife,
who went missing ten years ago.

20:25.098 --> 20:27.059
[tender instrumental music playing]

20:28.310 --> 20:29.228
[Chae-ok] This here.

20:30.687 --> 20:32.898
Is this one of your drawings
from a year ago?

20:34.608 --> 20:35.776
Yes, that's mine.

20:36.360 --> 20:39.071
I'm guessing you know
the woman in this drawing, then?

20:39.613 --> 20:42.032
I want to know how do…
I mean, when did you…

20:45.452 --> 20:47.537
How do you know her,
and do you know where she is?

20:49.122 --> 20:51.291
How do you know this woman, may I ask?

20:57.506 --> 20:58.423
She's my mother.

21:05.472 --> 21:07.266
[breathing shakily]

21:07.349 --> 21:08.517
So what do you know?

21:09.977 --> 21:12.938
Can you give me any information
on where she is right now?

21:13.438 --> 21:14.564
It would help me.

21:18.193 --> 21:19.361
I want to know everything.

21:22.823 --> 21:23.657
[groaning]

21:23.740 --> 21:25.075
[creature growling]

21:25.158 --> 21:26.868
[spluttering]

21:27.953 --> 21:29.454
[grunting]

21:31.832 --> 21:33.166
- [screaming]
- [grunting]

21:35.168 --> 21:37.212
- [woman sobbing]
- [whimpering]

21:44.177 --> 21:45.387
[bell ringing]

21:46.221 --> 21:47.556
[heavy footsteps stomping]

21:53.145 --> 21:55.522
It moves so fast without a sound.

21:56.398 --> 21:57.983
What a dangerous creature.

21:59.318 --> 22:01.695
It's so… powerful.

22:03.655 --> 22:06.742
How many more of these creatures
can you create for the emperor?

22:09.745 --> 22:10.662
Well,

22:11.371 --> 22:13.749
this is the only one that was a success,

22:14.541 --> 22:15.709
so it's hard to say.

22:18.086 --> 22:20.505
All the other test subjects either died

22:20.589 --> 22:22.924
or became deformed
as the serum took over them.

22:23.008 --> 22:24.176
[tuts, sighs]

22:24.259 --> 22:27.012
You must find a way
to make more of these creatures.

22:27.095 --> 22:30.265
The emperor needs to know
what we have created

22:30.349 --> 22:32.934
so that he can be victorious
and win this war.

22:33.018 --> 22:34.644
[rapid footsteps approaching]

22:38.315 --> 22:39.900
[tense music playing]

22:44.363 --> 22:45.947
We're done for today.

22:46.031 --> 22:48.408
Return the rest of the subjects
to their cells.

22:49.284 --> 22:51.661
I have other business to attend to.

22:52.329 --> 22:53.246
Excuse me.

23:00.462 --> 23:01.546
Take them back.

23:01.630 --> 23:02.881
[prisoners grunting]

23:07.719 --> 23:09.638
[tense music building]

23:13.392 --> 23:14.559
[snarling gently]

23:27.114 --> 23:28.448
[low growling]

23:29.116 --> 23:30.951
[snarling softly]

23:33.870 --> 23:35.872
[sentimental piano music playing]

23:36.748 --> 23:37.916
Look, I'm sorry.

23:38.750 --> 23:39.668
But I don't know.

23:39.751 --> 23:41.878
I thought you said you drew this picture.

23:44.214 --> 23:45.924
Yes, it's true. I did draw that.

23:47.300 --> 23:49.010
I just don't know where she is.

23:55.392 --> 23:56.810
I don't know what happened to her.

23:58.311 --> 23:59.938
Do you really not know anything?

24:06.820 --> 24:09.448
I've spent ten desperate years
looking for her.

24:11.700 --> 24:14.119
I spent three years
investigating in Manchuria.

24:16.496 --> 24:19.583
Then this portrait came into
my possession, and that's when I…

24:20.125 --> 24:21.460
I came back here to Joseon

24:21.543 --> 24:24.045
to find the person who might know
what really happened to her.

24:29.718 --> 24:31.595
Are you sure you don't know where she is?

24:32.512 --> 24:33.597
I'm sorry, I don't.

24:44.524 --> 24:46.359
[sentimental piano music continues]

24:54.201 --> 24:55.994
[sentimental piano music continues]

25:15.555 --> 25:17.599
[breathing shakily]

25:22.437 --> 25:23.522
[music fades]

25:26.608 --> 25:27.901
Know how to pull a rickshaw?

25:30.529 --> 25:32.447
I've, uh, I've only done it twice, sir.

25:34.366 --> 25:35.408
Come here, then.

25:44.543 --> 25:46.711
[sentimental string music playing]

25:46.795 --> 25:47.879
From now on,

25:48.797 --> 25:49.965
you will lead them.

25:51.216 --> 25:53.969
As a man, it's your responsibility

25:54.052 --> 25:56.429
to take these kids out of here.
Understand?

26:04.312 --> 26:07.315
Let's play a game.
A little hide-and-seek, okay?

26:08.316 --> 26:10.902
Don't let any Japanese soldiers
find you, huh?

26:11.820 --> 26:13.738
Wait until the rickshaw stops moving.

26:14.614 --> 26:17.576
Whoever is the most quiet…
will win the game.

26:25.750 --> 26:27.335
And if you all remain hidden,

26:28.169 --> 26:29.838
I will give you all one of these.

26:30.338 --> 26:31.172
Can you do that?

26:32.382 --> 26:33.216
Here.

26:34.801 --> 26:35.802
What's the plan now?

26:36.761 --> 26:38.680
We're gonna get these kids
out of here first.

26:41.600 --> 26:43.101
That's our first priority.

26:43.810 --> 26:44.811
Right, Yoon Chae-ok?

26:51.026 --> 26:52.110
[music fades]

26:52.193 --> 26:53.194
What's that?

26:54.112 --> 26:55.363
Sachimoto's studio?

26:55.447 --> 26:58.533
Yes, sir. I'm quite sure.
I heard a girl scream from inside.

26:58.617 --> 27:00.660
- [sighs]
- [tense music playing]

27:12.213 --> 27:13.465
Mr. Sachimoto.

27:15.467 --> 27:16.551
Mr. Sachimoto!

27:18.887 --> 27:19.763
Open it!

27:28.730 --> 27:30.273
[music intensifies]

27:41.368 --> 27:43.495
[heartbeat rhythm echoing]

27:43.578 --> 27:45.038
[tense music continues]

27:52.253 --> 27:53.463
[soldier] Mr. Sachimoto!

27:53.963 --> 27:55.715
[unsettling music playing]

27:55.799 --> 27:57.050
[footsteps approaching]

28:08.603 --> 28:10.397
[heartbeat rhythm echoing]

28:15.485 --> 28:16.444
Is something wrong?

28:16.528 --> 28:19.489
Where are you headed to
this evening, huh? You're up late.

28:20.782 --> 28:22.200
Uh, why do you ask, sir?

28:22.784 --> 28:26.246
[sighs] It looks like, uh,
a couple kids escaped tonight.

28:28.623 --> 28:29.457
[Sachimoto] And?

28:30.125 --> 28:31.543
One of my corporals heard

28:31.626 --> 28:32.961
a little girl screaming.

28:33.503 --> 28:35.588
It sounded like it came from your studio.

28:38.216 --> 28:40.802
I don't know about that.
I was cleaning up a little.

28:42.303 --> 28:44.973
Can we take a little peek
inside your cart, then?

28:50.186 --> 28:51.938
[unsettling music playing]

29:11.332 --> 29:12.667
[music fades]

29:13.501 --> 29:14.961
[dramatic music playing]

29:21.259 --> 29:23.178
[Tae-sang] Look straight ahead
and don't hesitate.

29:23.261 --> 29:25.889
Just keep running.
Don't look back, you hear me?

29:25.972 --> 29:27.015
Go past the main gate

29:27.098 --> 29:29.350
and don't stop running
no matter what, you got that?

29:35.064 --> 29:36.191
Hold on.

29:44.741 --> 29:46.326
Be confident and stay strong.

29:46.993 --> 29:50.747
You're just… a rickshaw puller
doing his night run, nothing else.

29:50.830 --> 29:51.748
You'll be okay.

29:52.999 --> 29:54.042
[chuckles softly]

29:55.168 --> 29:56.252
[taps of encouragement]

30:20.193 --> 30:21.486
You, open the gates!

30:31.371 --> 30:32.205
Hey!

30:32.288 --> 30:33.164
Wait.

30:37.168 --> 30:38.086
[car horn honks]

30:40.463 --> 30:43.550
Go tell Director Ichiro
a woman from Honmachi's here for him.

30:43.633 --> 30:44.467
[man] Yes, sir!

30:55.228 --> 30:57.272
[boy crying]

31:04.362 --> 31:05.655
[crying continues]

31:11.619 --> 31:13.454
Would you like to check any other places?

31:17.083 --> 31:18.126
So tell me,

31:19.460 --> 31:20.962
do I need to check in with you

31:21.045 --> 31:24.048
every time I decide to clean up my room,
huh, sir?

31:25.216 --> 31:27.969
No. Enjoy your evening, Mr. Sachimoto.

31:35.643 --> 31:37.478
[janitor panting]

31:38.605 --> 31:39.689
[distant door opens]

31:40.356 --> 31:41.441
[cart rolling]

32:02.879 --> 32:03.963
[knocking on door]

32:04.047 --> 32:07.091
PAWNSHOP

32:30.323 --> 32:32.700
Tell Mr. Gu
to please come down here. Quickly.

32:33.284 --> 32:34.369
Yes, Mrs. Nawol.

32:37.664 --> 32:39.832
The other children, where are they now?

32:47.340 --> 32:49.509
[Mr. Gu] Oh my goodness.
There are two of them?

32:49.592 --> 32:50.843
[Mrs. Nawol] Come on out.

32:51.344 --> 32:53.930
- Here. Careful.
- Ah, careful. There you go.

32:54.013 --> 32:55.056
[Mrs. Nawol grunts]

32:55.139 --> 32:57.058
- You're all safe now.
- [Mr. Gu] Watch your step.

32:58.184 --> 33:00.103
- All right.
- You're safe. There you go.

33:00.186 --> 33:01.938
- You'll be safe here.
- Ah, okay.

33:04.524 --> 33:06.526
- [mysterious music playing]
- [straining]

33:11.155 --> 33:12.824
[Mr. Gu] Oh my goodness! Two more?

33:13.324 --> 33:15.201
[Mrs. Nawol] Oh my, come on out of there.

33:25.962 --> 33:27.755
Did Master Jang give you this?

33:28.548 --> 33:30.758
Do you know who won the game? Is it over?

33:30.842 --> 33:32.010
What game?

33:32.093 --> 33:33.928
We were playing hide-and-seek.

33:34.012 --> 33:36.639
The man said we could win
another can of cookies

33:36.723 --> 33:39.600
if we didn't get caught by
any Japanese soldiers.

33:42.270 --> 33:43.271
[Mrs. Nawol] I see.

33:43.354 --> 33:46.858
Yes, you won the game.
I'll make sure to get you more cookies.

33:49.694 --> 33:52.822
You must be hungry.
How about we make you something nice?

33:54.657 --> 33:56.409
- Yes, let's go. Let's go.
- Let's go.

33:56.492 --> 33:57.618
- Over here.
- Come now.

34:00.955 --> 34:03.291
The carotid artery
was severed in one blow.

34:03.374 --> 34:07.045
One of the children who escaped tonight
was a young teenage boy, sir.

34:07.128 --> 34:10.715
No. This was done by someone
skilled with knifework.

34:11.466 --> 34:14.469
See if there are any Josenjings
mixed with our soldiers.

34:14.552 --> 34:16.345
They could've entered the lab
together somehow.

34:16.429 --> 34:18.389
Yes, sir! Right away, Director.

34:24.812 --> 34:27.356
Sir, your guest from Honmachi
is waiting for you.

34:45.374 --> 34:47.835
My apologies for keeping you waiting,
Lady Maeda.

34:48.336 --> 34:51.255
There are some very urgent matters
that needed my attention.

34:52.590 --> 34:53.841
[tense music playing]

34:56.511 --> 34:59.806
May I ask what brings you
to the hospital at such a late hour?

35:00.598 --> 35:01.849
Jung Tae-sang.

35:03.101 --> 35:04.185
I think

35:04.685 --> 35:07.355
he broke into the hospital
and is here right now.

35:09.107 --> 35:09.982
PRISON

35:10.066 --> 35:12.902
[man] Based on the information
we've gathered so far,

35:12.985 --> 35:15.988
it seems that Myeong-ja's being held
in the basement in the second level.

35:16.072 --> 35:18.449
And do we know
if there are other Joseon citizens

35:18.533 --> 35:20.243
imprisoned within that area?

35:20.326 --> 35:21.410
It seems so.

35:24.580 --> 35:25.748
We need to hurry.

35:25.832 --> 35:27.750
We only have three hours
until the sun rises.

35:27.834 --> 35:30.837
If we don't get Myeong-ja out by morning,
everything will get more challenging.

35:30.920 --> 35:32.088
Understood.

35:32.171 --> 35:34.507
I'm sorry, but my shift is almost over.

35:34.590 --> 35:37.760
They might start getting suspicious
if I don't get back in time.

35:37.844 --> 35:39.387
I understand. You should probably go.

35:40.721 --> 35:44.767
If you are able to get down there,
can you look for my little brother?

35:46.644 --> 35:47.895
His name is Oh Sang-deok.

35:49.522 --> 35:51.190
He's in his early twenties,
average height.

35:51.274 --> 35:53.109
He has a black birthmark
over his right ear.

35:53.192 --> 35:55.111
It's about the size of a small thumb.

35:56.154 --> 35:59.073
- Can you please be on the lookout?
- We will look for him.

36:00.032 --> 36:01.117
I give you my word.

36:02.160 --> 36:03.244
I'd be very grateful.

36:04.579 --> 36:07.248
I also think
that I should say goodbye for now.

36:08.541 --> 36:12.587
I truly hope… that you achieve
everything you are hoping to.

36:23.598 --> 36:24.557
[door closes]

36:25.141 --> 36:27.602
All right. We should be
getting a move on as well.

36:28.978 --> 36:31.689
Actually, I think
you should both leave the hospital.

36:32.899 --> 36:34.317
Although we found Sachimoto,

36:34.400 --> 36:36.777
we weren't able to get
any intel on your mother.

36:36.861 --> 36:39.572
Therefore, I don't have
any issues ending our contract.

36:40.156 --> 36:41.824
I appreciate everything you've done.

36:43.034 --> 36:46.579
So in that case… I should
hold on to this for the time being.

36:48.164 --> 36:50.625
No, the deal also included
getting Myeong-ja out of here.

36:50.708 --> 36:52.752
Well, yes, thanks to you,
we know where Myeong-ja is.

36:52.835 --> 36:54.086
That's more than enough.

36:55.379 --> 36:58.341
No, it's not.
You kept your end of the deal, and so, um,

36:58.424 --> 37:00.051
we'll keep our promise as well.

37:00.134 --> 37:03.179
- As I said, you've fulfilled your promise.
- [grunts]

37:03.971 --> 37:05.389
[tender instrumental music playing]

37:05.473 --> 37:07.975
You can be really annoying at times,
you know that?

37:08.059 --> 37:10.728
Why do you always keep
making me repeat myself to you?

37:12.230 --> 37:13.731
Do I really do that?

37:18.152 --> 37:19.487
I'll lead the way, okay?

37:21.197 --> 37:22.782
Try not to get lost, Master Jang.

37:26.911 --> 37:29.247
Uh… please excuse her.

37:30.164 --> 37:34.210
Just know that my daughter
takes her promises very seriously.

37:34.293 --> 37:35.962
[chuckling] Yes, I see. Hmm.

37:40.800 --> 37:42.134
[dramatic music playing]

37:56.274 --> 37:57.942
That really hurt. All right. Ah!

38:07.827 --> 38:10.621
- [Jun-taek] What's with those soldiers?
- I'll explain everything later.

38:11.122 --> 38:12.164
Come on, hurry.

38:13.916 --> 38:14.875
Are you all right?

38:15.918 --> 38:17.086
Um, why wouldn't I be?

38:21.007 --> 38:22.967
So, uh, are we all going down this way?

38:26.887 --> 38:29.265
- It's dark. I can't see anything.
- [sighs]

38:33.394 --> 38:34.562
[dramatic music continues]

38:34.645 --> 38:36.897
Do you even have any idea
where this leads to?

38:37.398 --> 38:38.774
I guess we're all going in.

38:42.028 --> 38:43.279
We don't have any time to lose.

38:44.780 --> 38:47.199
I'm right behind you.
I just wanna have a quick look around.

38:47.283 --> 38:48.451
I'll follow you in a minute.

39:03.341 --> 39:04.633
[music fades]

39:09.847 --> 39:11.182
[tense music playing]

39:13.017 --> 39:14.185
[scabbard hitting ground]

39:24.904 --> 39:27.114
I see someone
on the rooftop of the hospital ward.

39:27.198 --> 39:28.699
Can you confirm for me, sir?

39:28.783 --> 39:30.284
[man over radio] Keep an eye on it!

39:30.951 --> 39:31.952
Yes, sir!

39:43.506 --> 39:44.965
[Tae-sang grunting]

39:46.717 --> 39:48.969
[groans softly, breathes heavily]

39:52.056 --> 39:54.475
I sprained my ankle.
I'm fine, though, seriously.

39:58.979 --> 39:59.980
[gasps]

40:04.485 --> 40:05.444
[Jun-taek grunts]

40:06.112 --> 40:07.029
[sighs]

40:09.073 --> 40:09.907
[gasps]

40:16.122 --> 40:18.040
What is this monstrosity?

40:22.169 --> 40:23.421
Right this way.

40:36.976 --> 40:38.561
[tense music building]

40:40.980 --> 40:43.399
FOR THE INDEPENDENCE OF KOREA

40:47.194 --> 40:48.863
[whistle blowing]

40:50.531 --> 40:51.866
[tense music intensifies]

40:55.161 --> 40:56.328
[whistle blowing]

40:56.412 --> 40:58.789
- [man 1] Everyone out.
- [man 2] Hurry up! Move!

40:58.873 --> 41:00.624
- [man 3] Hurry!
- [man 2] This is an emergency!

41:00.708 --> 41:03.294
- We're moving immediately. Follow me.
- Yes, sir!

41:03.377 --> 41:05.171
[indistinct rallying calls]

41:08.841 --> 41:10.342
Get up! Get up now!

41:11.051 --> 41:12.595
That includes you, Josenjing!

41:12.678 --> 41:13.637
Get up now!

41:14.180 --> 41:16.056
We have an intruder in the hospital.

41:16.140 --> 41:19.685
Disease Control Platoon, arm yourselves
and get downstairs. That's an order!

41:19.768 --> 41:22.146
- Hurry, move out!
- [soldiers] Yes, sir!

41:22.229 --> 41:23.689
[dramatic music playing]

41:31.822 --> 41:34.492
I have no excuses
for the security breach tonight.

41:34.575 --> 41:37.286
Nothing like this
has ever happened to us before.

41:37.369 --> 41:39.371
Sorry for the inconvenience, Lady Maeda.

41:39.455 --> 41:41.707
[siren wailing in distance]

41:41.790 --> 41:45.711
Those who believe they are untouchable
let their guard down more easily.

41:45.794 --> 41:48.047
Perhaps this was a lesson, Mr. Ichiro.

41:48.130 --> 41:50.216
Now, to what I have entrusted to you,

41:50.299 --> 41:53.802
until that woman
has finally given birth to her child,

41:54.428 --> 41:56.597
she must remain unharmed until then.

41:57.181 --> 41:58.933
She is to remain hidden here.

42:00.100 --> 42:01.727
You must not disappoint me.

42:04.355 --> 42:07.107
Although,
you already know this, Mr. Ichiro.

42:08.734 --> 42:09.735
Yes, Lady Maeda.

42:10.569 --> 42:12.238
It will all be taken care of. I promise.

42:20.204 --> 42:21.121
Open it!

42:21.205 --> 42:22.957
- [keys jangling]
- [woman whimpering]

42:25.251 --> 42:26.168
Come out of there.

42:26.252 --> 42:27.711
[unsettling music playing]

42:29.713 --> 42:30.965
You better come out now!

42:31.048 --> 42:32.925
[breathing shakily]

42:33.759 --> 42:35.052
Drag her out of there.

42:35.719 --> 42:38.264
[panting fearfully] No! No!

42:38.347 --> 42:39.723
I don't wanna die! [yelps]

42:39.807 --> 42:41.016
Please don't kill me!

42:41.100 --> 42:42.184
[wailing]

42:42.268 --> 42:44.937
Let go! No! No!

42:45.020 --> 42:46.564
[screaming]

42:47.523 --> 42:49.984
Someone help! Please don't kill me!

42:50.067 --> 42:51.777
[screaming]

42:51.860 --> 42:53.779
- Let go!
- What will happen to us now?

42:53.862 --> 42:56.407
Someone help me! [yelping]

42:56.490 --> 42:57.950
[panting fearfully]

43:00.995 --> 43:02.955
[unsettling music playing]

43:06.792 --> 43:08.460
[Myeong-ja breathing heavily]

43:13.007 --> 43:14.174
[whimpering]

43:20.180 --> 43:23.017
[Myeong-ja in distance] No!
Don't kill me! Someone help!

43:23.100 --> 43:25.144
[creature growling softly]

43:25.227 --> 43:26.604
[Myeong-ja] Help!

43:26.687 --> 43:27.855
[creature snarling]

43:27.938 --> 43:30.482
[Myeong-ja whimpering]

43:31.775 --> 43:33.110
[wails]

43:34.278 --> 43:35.529
Let go!

43:39.033 --> 43:40.909
[creature growling softly]

43:41.619 --> 43:43.078
[elevator squeaking]

43:46.290 --> 43:48.459
[growling softly]

43:57.926 --> 43:59.261
[low growling]

44:07.811 --> 44:09.104
[mouth opening wetly]

44:09.188 --> 44:10.356
[snarling]

44:17.237 --> 44:18.906
[unsettling music continues]

44:22.701 --> 44:24.495
[low growling]

44:25.913 --> 44:27.289
[exhales]

44:28.165 --> 44:29.917
[guttural growling]

44:32.461 --> 44:34.213
[panicked breathing]

44:34.296 --> 44:35.547
[sobbing]

44:36.465 --> 44:38.634
I shouldn't be in here, sir. I'm pregnant!

44:38.717 --> 44:42.054
I can't stay here, sir.
Please listen to me. My baby could die!

44:43.347 --> 44:45.849
If you really wanna live,
you better stay quiet.

44:45.933 --> 44:48.477
I don't wanna hear
a peep out of you, got that?

44:48.560 --> 44:50.521
The quieter you are,
the safer you'll be in here,

44:50.604 --> 44:53.065
At least until
that illegitimate baby of yours is born.

44:54.149 --> 44:55.442
- [hits bars]
- [gasps]

44:56.652 --> 44:58.445
[whimpering]

44:59.738 --> 45:01.115
[sobbing]

45:16.588 --> 45:17.423
[music fades]

45:20.134 --> 45:21.343
[elevator bell dings]

45:22.302 --> 45:23.220
[officer sighs]

45:24.179 --> 45:25.180
[elevator clunking]

45:32.938 --> 45:34.356
[elevator bell dings]

45:42.823 --> 45:44.324
[tense music playing]

45:48.912 --> 45:51.290
[low growling]

45:53.751 --> 45:55.169
- [pained grunt]
- [shocked gasp]

45:55.753 --> 45:56.628
[spluttering]

45:58.213 --> 45:59.298
[creature snarling]

45:59.381 --> 46:00.799
[terrified yelling]

46:04.094 --> 46:06.138
[distant gunfire echoing]

46:06.221 --> 46:07.931
[dramatic music playing]

46:08.015 --> 46:09.349
[creature growling]

46:10.684 --> 46:12.102
[soldiers yelling]

46:15.189 --> 46:16.482
[screaming]

46:19.193 --> 46:20.527
[panicked breathing]

46:23.989 --> 46:26.116
[heavy footsteps thudding]

46:31.163 --> 46:32.623
[creature growling softly]

46:36.335 --> 46:37.586
[growling, snarls]

46:39.046 --> 46:43.634
Are you saying… the intruder somehow
found a way to the basement levels?

46:44.635 --> 46:46.136
They couldn't have, Director.

46:46.220 --> 46:49.681
From now on, monitor and guard
every single path that leads down here.

46:49.765 --> 46:51.767
I want guards at every hallway entrance.

46:51.850 --> 46:54.770
Any Joseon citizens from the outside
who have seen our labs

46:54.853 --> 46:56.146
must be detained at once.

46:56.230 --> 46:57.940
No one gets out of here alive.

46:58.774 --> 46:59.775
Do you understand?

47:00.359 --> 47:01.401
Yes, sir!

47:02.861 --> 47:04.279
[tense music playing]

47:06.490 --> 47:09.034
They must have found out
we're in the hospital. What should we do?

47:10.244 --> 47:11.829
What was that gunshot we heard?

47:12.412 --> 47:13.455
[Chae-ok] Whatever it was,

47:13.539 --> 47:16.124
I don't think it's possible
to use the emergency stairs anymore.

47:17.417 --> 47:18.377
So what do we do?

47:18.460 --> 47:20.879
Sachimoto had shown me
another way to get to Myeong-ja.

47:24.216 --> 47:25.092
[Sachimoto] Here.

47:25.175 --> 47:28.428
This leads to the laundry room
in the second-floor basement.

47:28.512 --> 47:31.890
They use it to send down surgical gowns
from the underground lab

47:31.974 --> 47:33.433
down to the laundry room,

47:34.309 --> 47:36.812
but it's wide enough
that you can walk through it.

47:37.855 --> 47:41.024
- Where exactly is that room located?
- Right across from here.

47:47.614 --> 47:49.283
[officer] Clean it up. Hurry!

47:50.951 --> 47:51.869
[soldier 1 groans]

47:58.584 --> 47:59.459
[groaning]

48:05.883 --> 48:07.634
[suspenseful music playing]

48:41.251 --> 48:42.836
Hey, are you feeling all right?

48:43.337 --> 48:44.421
Come on. Keep going.

48:46.548 --> 48:47.883
[clunking in distance]

48:53.764 --> 48:55.098
[tense music playing]

49:00.103 --> 49:02.522
- [officer] I want a thorough search!
- [soldiers] Yes, sir!

49:03.023 --> 49:04.650
[officer] Let's go! Move!

49:04.733 --> 49:06.777
This is an emergency! Get it together!

49:06.860 --> 49:08.028
[soldiers] Yes, sir!

49:49.486 --> 49:50.404
This way. Follow me.

49:52.948 --> 49:54.449
[tense music playing]

50:03.917 --> 50:04.793
[Tae-sang grunts]

50:07.629 --> 50:08.588
Shit.

50:13.176 --> 50:15.846
[grunts, breathes heavily]

50:15.929 --> 50:17.139
[pained gasp]

50:19.016 --> 50:21.601
We have to hurry.
There's a soldier following us.

50:21.685 --> 50:22.769
Keep moving.

50:22.853 --> 50:24.563
[tense music building]

50:45.917 --> 50:46.918
[Tae-sang groans]

50:48.420 --> 50:49.504
[pained groan]

50:53.133 --> 50:55.635
I'm not hurt.
I'm all right. Don't worry, I'm okay.

50:56.470 --> 50:59.848
- Are you all right, Chae-ok?
- Don't worry, Father. I'm okay.

51:03.143 --> 51:04.644
Um, are you okay?

51:11.985 --> 51:12.903
Don't move!

51:14.738 --> 51:15.822
[menacing music playing]

51:19.743 --> 51:20.911
[soldier] Hand it over.

51:21.411 --> 51:22.537
Hand it over!

51:24.873 --> 51:26.249
[dramatic music playing]

51:30.003 --> 51:31.630
Dirty Josenjing bastard!

51:32.589 --> 51:34.174
[distant gunshot echoing]

51:44.851 --> 51:46.394
[gunfire]

51:47.813 --> 51:48.855
[pained groaning]

51:49.731 --> 51:50.732
[creature screeches]

51:51.483 --> 51:52.484
[snarling]

51:52.567 --> 51:53.777
[soldier screaming]

51:54.444 --> 51:55.862
[creature snarling]

51:58.532 --> 51:59.533
Chae-ok!

52:05.372 --> 52:06.581
[soldier groaning]

52:19.177 --> 52:20.846
[soldier 1 screaming]

52:21.763 --> 52:23.056
[creature snarling]

52:23.140 --> 52:24.558
[soldier 2 whimpering]

52:26.643 --> 52:28.311
- [gunfire]
- [soldier 3 screams]

52:28.395 --> 52:29.729
[soldier 2 whimpering]

52:29.813 --> 52:31.356
[gunfire]

52:33.900 --> 52:34.943
[creature growls]

52:36.194 --> 52:37.112
[soldier 2 yelps]

52:37.195 --> 52:38.572
[terrified gasping]

52:52.377 --> 52:53.461
[gunshot]

52:55.338 --> 52:56.673
[soldier screams]

52:59.843 --> 53:01.011
[music fades]

53:01.720 --> 53:03.138
[soft growling]

53:03.847 --> 53:05.849
[guttural growling]

53:18.778 --> 53:20.655
[Tae-sang gasps]

53:25.368 --> 53:26.328
[relieved sigh]

53:32.083 --> 53:33.460
[panting, pained grunt]

53:37.714 --> 53:39.049
[Tae-sang panting]

53:44.930 --> 53:45.847
Heh…

53:46.640 --> 53:47.849
[tense music playing]

53:53.063 --> 53:54.522
[soldier breathing heavily]

53:55.273 --> 53:56.858
Please! Please help me!

53:57.359 --> 53:58.568
That thing…

53:59.402 --> 54:00.445
that monster,

54:00.528 --> 54:01.863
it's on its way here!

54:05.367 --> 54:06.785
[suspenseful music playing]

54:12.999 --> 54:14.542
[elevator rumbling]

54:27.639 --> 54:28.932
[elevator clunking]

54:34.104 --> 54:35.855
[dramatic music playing]

54:35.939 --> 54:37.607
[breathing shakily]

54:44.906 --> 54:46.449
[low growling]

54:49.828 --> 54:51.496
[low growling]

54:53.957 --> 54:56.209
[breathing heavily]

54:58.128 --> 54:59.004
[yelps]

55:00.088 --> 55:01.339
[chokes]

55:01.423 --> 55:02.590
[music fades]

55:06.511 --> 55:08.471
[tender instrumental music playing]

55:14.602 --> 55:15.603
[pained grunt]

55:26.323 --> 55:27.657
[music fades]

55:43.131 --> 55:45.383
You shouldn't be so reckless
when you're hurt like this.

55:46.760 --> 55:48.136
[Tae-sang breathes shakily]

55:48.928 --> 55:50.138
I wasn't reckless.

55:51.014 --> 55:52.140
I was trying to…

55:52.849 --> 55:56.561
to be brave and, uh…
I just really wanted to win in the end.

56:12.786 --> 56:17.374
Just so you know, your friend left us.
He may have to find a way out on his own.

56:18.333 --> 56:20.043
Well, he and I did agree

56:20.126 --> 56:22.754
it would be every man for himself
if necessary.

56:25.965 --> 56:28.593
- Are you sure you'll be fine?
- Of course I will.

56:30.053 --> 56:32.472
Let's go.
It's about time we find Myeong-ja.

56:35.683 --> 56:37.769
Listen, Master Jang. We need to split up.

56:38.603 --> 56:40.772
Go to the second-floor prison
and check for Myeong-Ja.

56:41.356 --> 56:43.024
I'll go down to the third-level basement.

56:43.108 --> 56:44.567
I can check the third level.

56:44.651 --> 56:47.028
Listen to me. He's too hurt to go alone.

56:47.529 --> 56:49.030
Please stay with Master Jang.

56:49.114 --> 56:50.448
But, Father…

56:50.532 --> 56:51.658
Do as I say.

56:52.742 --> 56:54.369
This is the most efficient way.

56:55.870 --> 56:59.624
All right, we'll meet in one hour
at the place we agreed to before.

56:59.707 --> 57:03.128
If for any… reason I'm late,
don't wait. Understand?

57:03.837 --> 57:04.921
You know the drill.

57:05.004 --> 57:06.214
Please be careful.

57:17.100 --> 57:18.309
[Tae-sang sighs]

57:18.852 --> 57:21.688
You can go with your father.
I'll take this gun here.

57:22.188 --> 57:23.398
I'll just go on alone.

57:25.108 --> 57:25.942
Just follow me.

57:28.778 --> 57:29.904
[door opens]

57:29.988 --> 57:30.905
[sighs]

57:48.089 --> 57:50.091
[Tae-sang breathing heavily]

57:54.721 --> 57:57.307
A while back,
I heard several gunshots being fired.

57:57.390 --> 58:00.727
Why do I get the sense
there's something else going on in here?

58:02.562 --> 58:04.272
Just stay here and wait for me.

58:17.702 --> 58:18.870
[electricity crackling]

58:19.662 --> 58:20.872
[ominous music playing]

58:21.748 --> 58:22.665
[exhales sharply]

58:29.297 --> 58:30.965
[suspenseful music playing]

58:31.591 --> 58:33.092
[choked gasping in distance]

58:34.260 --> 58:35.220
[distant thud]

58:37.013 --> 58:38.640
[choked gasping]

58:39.390 --> 58:40.683
[choked gasping]

58:40.767 --> 58:42.435
[heavy footsteps squelching]

58:55.949 --> 58:57.367
[dramatic music playing]

59:00.078 --> 59:01.079
[soft growling]

59:12.215 --> 59:13.091
[creature huffs]

59:14.425 --> 59:15.885
[growling]

59:40.159 --> 59:42.787
[roaring]

59:44.956 --> 59:46.332
[dramatic music continues]

01:00:46.225 --> 01:00:47.644
[dramatic music fades]

01:00:47.727 --> 01:00:49.896
[unsettling instrumental music playing]

01:03:11.037 --> 01:03:13.039
[music fades out]
